        <!--
            NSUserTrackingUsageDescription intentionally removed.

            ATT was deleted from the user flow in 1.7.3 (we never present the
            prompt). Keeping the usage-description key without a prompt is an
            orphan that App Review may flag during a privacy-sensitive cycle.
            Attribution runs on SKAN postbacks + Apple Search Ads AdServices
            token instead, neither of which requires ATT.
        -->
        <!--
            ONDA itself does NOT use the device location. This usage string
            is here only because Apple's static analyzer requires it: the
            OneSignal SDK we use for push notifications links CoreLocation
            internally even though we never request authorization or read
            coordinates. Without this key the App Store upload throws
            ITMS-90683 'Missing purpose string'.
        -->
        <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
        <string>ONDA does not request your location. This entry is required by Apple because a push-notification SDK links the location framework.</string>
        <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
        <string>ONDA uses the microphone during emotional check-ins to analyze your voice and provide personalized wellness recommendations.</string>
        <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
        <string>ONDA uses the camera for an optional eye scan that reads gaze and blink patterns to personalize practices. Frames are processed on-device and not stored.</string>
        <key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
        <string>ONDA uses your heart rate data to provide personalized meditation and breathing exercises that adapt to your stress levels and wellness state.</string>
        <key>NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription</key>
        <string>ONDA tracks your mindfulness sessions and workout data in Apple Health to help you monitor your wellness progress.</string>
